+## Amendment: lazy storage is typed at module boundaries (2026-11-14, #1752)
+
+The lazy representation owner exposes its initializer key and the two
+storage states as a Pending/Ready enum: pending (a callable or poisoned/null
+initializer) and ready (a required payload and no active initializer).
+The enum owns required-member queries; independent booleans cannot describe
+an impossible third or fourth state. Declaration generation
+consumes this schema and the shared held-value key, instead of emitting any
+or keeping another property catalog. Lowering uses the same initializer key.
+The runtime helpers retain their established layout; a regression forces
+Rust-generated LazyCell and LazyLock values and checks both actual states
+against the declarations, testing the necessary JS-runtime mirror.
+
+Strict TypeScript callers accept numeric and structured payloads and reject
+wrong initializer returns, wrong payloads, and an object with neither state.
+Mutations make the ready payload optional or erase the initializer result
+type. Runtime representation is unchanged, ADR 0262 case A.
